# Plan-script run artefacts — LEGACY LOCATION.
#
# plan_start_log (CLAUDE/Plan/_planlib.inc.bash) now writes each run's tee'd log, and any
# report the run produces, to untracked/plan-runs/<plan>/<script>/<timestamp>/ at the repo
# root. It no longer writes anything beside the plan's tracked files.
#
# This rule stays for the <script>-runs/ directories earlier runs already left on disk, so
# they keep being ignored rather than appearing in git status. Safe to delete once those
# are gone.
#
# WHY THE MOVE. These logs are NEVER committed, deliberately: a plan run streams live
# ansible output that can carry vault-decrypted values. The rule now lives in the LOCATION
# rather than in this glob — untracked/ is excluded wholesale and is self-excluding, so a
# log there cannot reach an index by accident, whereas this pattern held only while the
# directory kept a name that still matched it.
#
# And this file used to say the repo had no run-log secret scrubber. It has one —
# scripts/lib/run-log-scrub.bash, built by Plan 00121 with its own QA gate — but that is
# wired into the VM lab's run logs, NOT into these. The accurate statement is "plan run
# logs are unscrubbed", not "this repo has no scrubber". If they ever need committing,
# wire that scrubber in FIRST, in the same change — never the other way round.
#
# See CLAUDE/PlanScriptStandards.md R4 and R10.
*-runs/
